    {
      "title": "Chapter 2 query-building core",
      "sourceType": "lecture",
      "body": "Relational algebra turns an information request into a typed pipeline: filter qualifying tuples, combine related relations, and project the requested attributes. Set operators work on compatible relations, while every intermediate result remains a relation.",
      "teaching": [
        "Start from the requested output attributes.",
        "Identify which relation owns each predicate attribute.",
        "Join only when the question needs facts from more than one relation.",
        "Apply selection before projection if the predicate needs an attribute that would otherwise be removed.",
        "Check operand compatibility before union, intersection, or difference."
      ],
